text:
VAR (Vector AutoRegressive) is a multivariate1 linear time series model, designed to capture the joint dynamics2 of multiple time series through an **interconnected system*.
VARs treat each endogenous variable3 in the system as a function of lagged values of all endogenous variables by default; plus exogenous variables only when explicitly added.
VARs offer a simple and flexible alternative to traditional multiple equation models.


3.1.1 A closer look: joint dynamics, interconnected system and endogeneity
In a VAR the variables are not studied side by side: they form a single system in which each one both drives and is driven by the others.
The interconnection is neither a one-off cross-effect nor unidirectional, it is mutual. Each variable enters the other’s equation, so influence runs in both directions and it propagates forward indefinitely. Neither variable can be held exogenous on RHS: this reciprocal dependence is exactly what endogeneity means here.
Example:
To fix ideas, let inflation (\(\pi\)) and GDP each depend on both their own lag and the other’s lag. Since the true data-generating process is unknown, the relationship is left as a generic function:
\[
\begin{aligned}
\pi_t &= f(\pi_{t-1},\, gdp_{t-1}) \\
gdp_t &= f(gdp_{t-1},\, \pi_{t-1})
\end{aligned}
\]
Following a single cross-channel makes the mechanism visible and more intuitive. Take the \(gdp \to \pi\) link (own-lag effects run in parallel, in exactly the same way):
\[
gdp_{t-1} \;\rightarrow\; \pi_t \;\rightarrow\; gdp_{t+1} \;\rightarrow\; \pi_{t+2} \;\rightarrow\; gdp_{t+3} \;\rightarrow\; \cdots
\]
This single thread, though, understates the structure. Own lags run alongside the cross-links, and an own lag is itself a product of the other variable one period earlier: \(gdp_{t-1}\) already carries \(\pi_{t-2}\). Every value is therefore fed, at every period, by both variables at once, as shown in the animation below, where horizontal arrows are own lags (persistence); diagonal arrows are cross-lags (spillovers).
This self-sustaining feedback loop is what makes the system genuinely joint, and it is the aspect most often underestimated when first learning VAR.

{
  const GDP = 0, PI = 1;
  const periods = ["t\u22121", "t", "t+1", "t+2"];
  const N = periods.length;

  const colGDP = "#4c78a8", colPI = "#e45756";
  const faint = "#ececec", firedCol = "#f6c667", hotArrow = "#f0a202";
  const shockCol = "#f0a202";
  const coldFill = "#f5f5f5", coldStroke = "#cfcfcf";
  const colOf = r =&gt; (r === GDP ? colGDP : colPI);

  const width = 680, height = 300;
  const mL = 88, mR = 30;
  const dx = (width - mL - mR) / (N - 1);
  const legendY = 22, periodY = 58, yTop = 104, yBot = 224, captionY = 288;
  const R = 15;
  const x = i =&gt; mL + i * dx;
  const yOf = r =&gt; (r === GDP ? yTop : yBot);

  const frames = [
    {type:"shock", caption:"A shock hits GDP at t\u22121."},
    {type:"trans", col:0, caption:"It carries into GDP (own lag) and spills into \u03C0 (cross-lag) \u2014 both now move."},
    {type:"trans", col:1, caption:"Now each variable feeds both: all four channels fire at once."},
    {type:"trans", col:2, caption:"\u2026and again \u2014 the feedback loop sustains itself, forward without end."},
    {type:"hold",  caption:"Every value is fed by both variables \u2014 one joint, interconnected system."},
    {type:"hold",  caption:"Every value is fed by both variables \u2014 one joint, interconnected system."}
  ];
  const total = frames.length;

  function stateAt(f) {
    const hot = [Array(N).fill(false), Array(N).fill(false)];
    hot[GDP][0] = true;
    const fired = new Set();
    let current = [];
    for (let idx = 1; idx &lt;= f && idx &lt; total; idx++) {
      const fr = frames[idx];
      if (fr.type !== "trans") continue;
      const c = fr.col;
      const arrowsThis = [];
      for (let r = 0; r &lt; 2; r++) {
        if (hot[r][c]) {
          arrowsThis.push([c, r, c + 1, GDP]);
          arrowsThis.push([c, r, c + 1, PI]);
        }
      }
      hot[GDP][c + 1] = true; hot[PI][c + 1] = true;
      if (idx === f) current = arrowsThis;
      else arrowsThis.forEach(a =&gt; fired.add(a.join(",")));
    }
    return {hot, fired, current, caption: frames[f].caption};
  }

  const container = d3.create("div").style("font-family", "system-ui, sans-serif");
  const controls = container.append("div")
    .style("display", "flex").style("gap", "6px").style("align-items", "center")
    .style("margin-bottom", "6px");
  const mkBtn = (label) =&gt; controls.append("button").text(label)
    .style("padding", "3px 10px").style("font-size", "13px")
    .style("border", "1px solid #ccc").style("border-radius", "6px")
    .style("background", "#fff").style("cursor", "pointer");
  const playBtn = mkBtn("Pause");
  const resetBtn = mkBtn("Reset");
  const prevBtn = mkBtn("\u2039");
  const nextBtn = mkBtn("\u203A");
  const holder = container.append("div");

  let f = 0, playing = true;

  function drawArrow(svg, i0, r0, i1, r1, mode) {
    const x0 = x(i0), y0 = yOf(r0), x1 = x(i1), y1 = yOf(r1);
    const a = Math.atan2(y1 - y0, x1 - x0);
    const sx = x0 + R * Math.cos(a), sy = y0 + R * Math.sin(a);
    const ex = x1 - (R + 5) * Math.cos(a), ey = y1 - (R + 5) * Math.sin(a);
    const col = mode === "hot" ? hotArrow : mode === "fired" ? firedCol : faint;
    const w = mode === "hot" ? 3.5 : mode === "fired" ? 2.5 : 1.2;
    svg.append("line")
      .attr("x1", sx).attr("y1", sy).attr("x2", ex).attr("y2", ey)
      .attr("stroke", col).attr("stroke-width", w)
      .attr("opacity", mode === "faint" ? 0.6 : 1)
      .attr("marker-end", "url(#ah-" + mode + ")");
  }

  function update() {
    const st = stateAt(f);
    holder.selectAll("*").remove();
    const svg = holder.append("svg")
      .attr("viewBox", [0, 0, width, height])
      .attr("width", width)
      .attr("style", "max-width:100%;height:auto;");

    const defs = svg.append("defs");
    [["faint", faint], ["fired", firedCol], ["hot", hotArrow]].forEach(([id, c]) =&gt; {
      defs.append("marker").attr("id", "ah-" + id)
        .attr("viewBox", "0 0 10 10").attr("refX", 9).attr("refY", 5)
        .attr("markerWidth", 7).attr("markerHeight", 7).attr("orient", "auto")
        .append("path").attr("d", "M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z").attr("fill", c);
    });

    // row baselines + labels (pi bigger)
    [["GDP", GDP, 16], ["\u03C0", PI, 26]].forEach(([lab, r, fs]) =&gt; {
      svg.append("line").attr("x1", mL - 20).attr("x2", width - mR)
        .attr("y1", yOf(r)).attr("y2", yOf(r)).attr("stroke", "#f2f2f2");
      svg.append("text").attr("x", mL - 34).attr("y", yOf(r) + fs / 3)
        .attr("text-anchor", "end").attr("font-weight", "bold")
        .attr("font-size", fs).attr("fill", colOf(r)).text(lab);
    });

    periods.forEach((p, i) =&gt; {
      svg.append("text").attr("x", x(i)).attr("y", periodY)
        .attr("text-anchor", "middle").attr("font-size", 12).attr("fill", "#999").text(p);
    });

    // faint full lattice
    for (let i = 0; i &lt; N - 1; i++) {
      drawArrow(svg, i, GDP, i + 1, GDP, "faint");
      drawArrow(svg, i, PI,  i + 1, PI,  "faint");
      drawArrow(svg, i, GDP, i + 1, PI,  "faint");
      drawArrow(svg, i, PI,  i + 1, GDP, "faint");
    }
    // already-fired
    st.fired.forEach(k =&gt; {
      const a = k.split(",").map(Number);
      drawArrow(svg, a[0], a[1], a[2], a[3], "fired");
    });
    // current transition: all arrows together
    st.current.forEach(a =&gt; drawArrow(svg, a[0], a[1], a[2], a[3], "hot"));

    // nodes
    for (let r = 0; r &lt; 2; r++) {
      for (let i = 0; i &lt; N; i++) {
        const isHot = st.hot[r][i];
        svg.append("circle").attr("cx", x(i)).attr("cy", yOf(r)).attr("r", R)
          .attr("fill", isHot ? colOf(r) : coldFill)
          .attr("stroke", isHot ? colOf(r) : coldStroke).attr("stroke-width", 2);
      }
    }

    // prominent animated shock at frame 0
    if (frames[f].type === "shock") {
      const cx = x(0), cy = yOf(GDP);
      for (let idx = 0; idx &lt; 3; idx++) {
        const ring = svg.append("circle")
          .attr("cx", cx).attr("cy", cy).attr("r", R)
          .attr("fill", "none").attr("stroke", shockCol).attr("stroke-width", 3);
        ring.append("animate").attr("attributeName", "r")
          .attr("values", R + ";" + (R + 34)).attr("dur", "1.3s")
          .attr("begin", (idx * 0.43) + "s").attr("repeatCount", "indefinite");
        ring.append("animate").attr("attributeName", "opacity")
          .attr("values", "0.95;0").attr("dur", "1.3s")
          .attr("begin", (idx * 0.43) + "s").attr("repeatCount", "indefinite");
      }
      svg.append("circle").attr("cx", cx).attr("cy", cy).attr("r", R + 3)
        .attr("fill", colGDP).attr("stroke", shockCol).attr("stroke-width", 3);
      svg.append("text").attr("x", cx).attr("y", cy - R - 14)
        .attr("text-anchor", "middle").attr("font-size", 15)
        .attr("font-weight", "bold").attr("fill", shockCol).text("SHOCK!");
    }

    // legend (raised)
    const lx = width - mR - 250, ly = legendY;
    svg.append("line").attr("x1", lx).attr("y1", ly).attr("x2", lx + 24).attr("y2", ly)
      .attr("stroke", "#bbb").attr("stroke-width", 2).attr("marker-end", "url(#ah-faint)");
    svg.append("text").attr("x", lx + 30).attr("y", ly + 4).attr("font-size", 11).attr("fill", "#666").text("own lag");
    svg.append("line").attr("x1", lx + 92).attr("y1", ly - 6).attr("x2", lx + 116).attr("y2", ly + 6)
      .attr("stroke", "#bbb").attr("stroke-width", 2).attr("marker-end", "url(#ah-faint)");
    svg.append("text").attr("x", lx + 122).attr("y", ly + 4).attr("font-size", 11).attr("fill", "#666").text("cross-lag");
    svg.append("circle").attr("cx", lx + 196).attr("cy", ly).attr("r", 5)
      .attr("fill", "none").attr("stroke", shockCol).attr("stroke-width", 2);
    svg.append("text").attr("x", lx + 206).attr("y", ly + 4).attr("font-size", 11).attr("fill", "#666").text("shock");

    // caption + counter
    svg.append("text").attr("x", width / 2).attr("y", captionY)
      .attr("text-anchor", "middle").attr("font-size", 13).attr("fill", "#333").text(st.caption);
    svg.append("text").attr("x", width - mR).attr("y", captionY)
      .attr("text-anchor", "end").attr("font-size", 11).attr("fill", "#bbb")
      .text((f + 1) + "/" + total);
  }

  playBtn.on("click", () =&gt; { playing = !playing; playBtn.text(playing ? "Pause" : "Play"); });
  resetBtn.on("click", () =&gt; { f = 0; update(); });
  prevBtn.on("click", () =&gt; { playing = false; playBtn.text("Play"); f = (f - 1 + total) % total; update(); });
  nextBtn.on("click", () =&gt; { playing = false; playBtn.text("Play"); f = (f + 1) % total; update(); });

  const timer = setInterval(() =&gt; { if (playing) { f = (f + 1) % total; update(); } }, 1300);
  invalidation.then(() =&gt; clearInterval(timer));

  update();
  return container.node();
}
